From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 04:11:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Leave the static extension loader's visibility to the platform on Windows

The loader that package_build.py generates marks
duckdb_register_static_extensions() hidden whenever the compiler is GCC
or clang. MinGW's GCC targets PE/COFF, which has no symbol visibility,
so it drops the attribute and -Wattributes says so on every Windows
build. The attribute now applies off Windows only, the way duckdb.h
spells its own visibility macros; a Linux or macOS build keeps the
symbol hidden as before. The generator is upstream's, so the lasting fix
belongs in package_build.py; this patch reapplies after every
regeneration.

Carried here until upstream takes it; not proposed upstream yet.

---
 src/duckdb/generated_extension_loader_package_build.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/duckdb/generated_extension_loader_package_build.cpp b/src/duckdb/generated_extension_loader_package_build.cpp
index a1196a176a..6afd69a582 100644
--- a/src/duckdb/generated_extension_loader_package_build.cpp
+++ b/src/duckdb/generated_extension_loader_package_build.cpp
@@ -81,7 +81,7 @@ int32_t duckdb_extension_core_functions_describe(duckdb_extension_descriptor *de
 #endif
 
 #ifndef DUCKDB_STATIC_EXTENSION_LOADER_API
-#if defined(__GNUC__) || defined(__clang__)
+#if !defined(_WIN32) && (defined(__GNUC__) || defined(__clang__))
 #define DUCKDB_STATIC_EXTENSION_LOADER_API __attribute__((visibility("hidden")))
 #else
 #define DUCKDB_STATIC_EXTENSION_LOADER_API
